    <string name="param_desc_vsync">Syncs the game\'s frames with your screen\'s refresh rate to stop visual tearing. Leave it ON unless you see tearing or stutter.</string>
    <string name="param_desc_frames_queued">How many frames the game prepares ahead of what the screen shows. Lower numbers cut input lag; higher numbers can improve smoothness on weaker hardware.</string>
    <string name="param_desc_anisotropy">Sharpens floors and walls viewed at an angle. Higher values may use a little more GPU bandwidth. Takes effect on the next launch.</string>
    <string name="param_desc_vibration">Scales the gamepad vibration strength. 0% disables vibration. Takes effect immediately while the game is running.</string>
    <string name="param_desc_sharpen">Sharpens the upscaled image (the full strength range applies to every upscaler). Has no effect while the upscaler is OFF.</string>
    <string name="param_desc_sharpness">Strength of the sharpening pass (0.00–2.00). Only used when sharpening is ON.</string>
    <string name="param_desc_display_stretch">How the picture fills the screen: Fit keeps the aspect ratio and leaves black bars; Stretch fills the screen but distorts the picture; Crop to fill keeps the aspect ratio, scales the picture until it covers the whole screen and crops the overflow (no bars, no distortion, some edge vision is lost). Takes effect on the next launch.</string>
    <string name="param_skip_animations">Skip animations</string>
    <string name="param_desc_skip_animations">Skips the intro logos and opening videos, and lets you skip any in-game video with the X button. Same switches as the Patches page.</string>

